line  start window   clip tempo  text
   0   3.90   4.22   3.47  1.00  Look, friends! A little green pod is hanging from the branch.
   1   8.17   3.62   3.07  1.00  It's wiggling... wiggle, wiggle! Something is inside!
   2  11.84   7.38   2.43  1.00  What could be hiding in there? Can you guess?
   3  19.27   2.25   1.30  1.00  Crack! It's opening!
   4  21.57   3.87   2.92  1.00  Ta-da! It's me! I'm Bella the butterfly!
   5  25.49   5.94   4.99  1.00  My wings are all wet and crumpled. Let me dry them in the sun.
   6  31.48   5.44   4.29  1.00  Bella opens her wings, slowly, slowly... Wow! So many colours!
   7  36.97   3.68   2.53  1.00  Hi, Bella! I'm Bobo! Your wings are so pretty!
   8  40.70   2.64   1.89  1.00  What sound does a butterfly make?
   9  43.39   2.63   1.68  1.00  Shhh! Listen...
  10  46.07   5.47   4.52  1.00  Butterflies are very, very quiet. We just go flutter, flutter!
  11  51.59   7.17   4.22  1.00  Can you flutter like Bella? Flap your arms, softly. Flutter, flutter!
  12  58.81   3.56   2.41  1.00  Here are three amazing butterfly facts!
  13  62.42   4.76   3.81  1.00  Number one. Every butterfly starts as a tiny caterpillar!
  14  67.23   7.10   6.35  1.00  I was a tiny egg on a leaf. Then I was a hungry caterpillar! Munch, munch, munch!
  15  74.38   5.76   5.01  1.00  Then I made a cosy chrysalis, and I slept and changed inside.
  16  80.19   4.57   2.62  1.00  Egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, butterfly!
  17  84.81   3.74   2.79  1.00  Number two. Butterflies taste with their feet!
  18  88.60   5.85   4.30  1.00  I land on a flower, and my feet say... mmm! Sweet!
  19  94.50   5.41   4.46  1.00  Number three. Butterflies drink with a long, curly tongue, like a straw!
  20  99.96   6.68   5.73  1.00  I uncurl it, and sip, sip, sip the sweet flower juice. It's called nectar!
  21 106.69   5.32   2.87  1.00  Can you sip like a butterfly? Sip, sip, sip!
  22 112.06   3.21   2.26  1.00  Now Bella wants to go on a big journey.
  23 115.32   6.73   5.98  1.00  I want to fly to the Rainbow Garden! It has the most flowers in the whole world!
  24 122.10   6.21   5.26  1.00  But the Rainbow Garden is far away. Over the meadow, past the pond, and up the hill.
  25 128.36   2.28   1.53  1.00  We'll come with you, Bella!
  26 130.69   2.72   1.57  1.00  Yes! It's an adventure!
  27 133.46   4.84   3.39  1.00  Off they go! Bella flutters, and her friends walk along.
  28 138.35   3.13   2.58  1.00  Oh no! Here comes a big wind! Whoooosh!
  29 141.53   2.95   2.00  1.00  Help! The wind is pushing me!
  30 144.53   2.84   1.89  1.00  Bella! Hold on to the flower!
  31 147.42   3.83   2.88  1.00  Bella holds on tight, and waits... and waits...
  32 151.30   2.98   1.53  1.00  The wind stops. Phew!
  33 154.33   4.72   3.57  1.00  I'm OK! When the wind is big, I hold on and wait.
  34 159.10   4.20   3.05  1.00  Now they walk past the pond. But look at the sky!
  35 163.35   3.47   2.92  1.00  Big grey clouds! Pitter, patter... it's raining!
  36 166.87   6.24   5.29  1.00  Oh no! Butterflies can't fly in the rain! Wet wings are too heavy!
  37 173.16   7.41   2.86  1.00  What can Bella do? How can she stay dry? Hmm...
  38 180.62   3.71   2.96  1.00  I know! Fly super fast, between the raindrops!
  39 184.38   3.56   2.81  1.00  Leo! Nobody can fly between the raindrops!
  40 187.99   2.58   1.23  1.00  Oops! Silly me!
  41 190.62   3.36   2.61  1.00  I have an idea! A big leaf, like an umbrella!
  42 194.03   4.81   3.86  1.00  Bobo holds a big green leaf, and everybody hides underneath.
  43 198.89   3.60   2.45  1.00  Thank you, Bobo! I'm nice and dry!
  44 202.54   3.66   2.71  1.00  The rain stops, the sun comes out, and look...
  45 206.25   4.87   3.42  1.00  A rainbow! Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple!
  46 211.17   3.85   2.90  1.00  Bella flies up the hill. She is getting tired.
  47 215.07   4.63   3.68  1.00  My wings are so tired. I need a little rest.
  48 219.75   3.36   2.41  1.00  Bella lands... right on Bobo's nose!
  49 223.16   3.10   2.15  1.00  Hee hee! It tickles! Ah... ah... ACHOO!
  50 226.31   5.30   3.75  1.00  Wheee! Hee hee! That's OK, Bobo. Now I'm ready to go!
  51 231.66   4.19   3.24  1.00  Little by little, flutter by flutter, Bella keeps going.
  52 235.90   3.21   2.26  1.00  And then... they reach the top of the hill.
  53 239.16   3.27   2.12  1.00  The Rainbow Garden! I made it!
  54 242.48   4.12   3.37  1.00  Look at all the flowers! Let's count the colours with Bella!
  55 246.65   5.18   2.23  1.00  One, red! Two, yellow! Three, purple!
  56 251.88   4.04   3.09  1.00  And look who lives here. Lots of butterfly friends!
  57 255.97   4.71   3.26  1.00  Hello, everybody! I flew all the way here!
  58 260.73   6.29   4.84  1.00  A big journey is done little by little. When it's hard, rest, and keep going!
  59 267.07   5.68   2.73  1.00  What is something YOU learned to do, little by little?
  60 272.80   2.89   1.94  1.00  Let's remember! Are you ready?
  61 275.74   6.71   2.26  1.00  What was Bella before she was a butterfly?
  62 282.50   3.90   2.45  1.00  A hungry caterpillar! Munch, munch!
  63 286.45   6.27   1.82  1.00  What do butterflies taste with?
  64 292.77   2.36   0.91  1.00  Their feet!
  65 295.18   6.75   2.30  1.00  What did Bella do when the big wind came?
  66 301.98   3.24   1.79  1.00  I held on, and waited!
  67 305.27   6.98   2.53  1.00  Can butterflies fly between the raindrops?
  68 312.30   3.65   2.20  1.00  No! Silly me! We used a big leaf!
  69 316.00   6.58   2.13  1.00  Where did Bella rest when she was tired?
